- `methodology/03a-decide-agent-vault-interaction.md` — the agent SOUL has a Tools section (required / optional / forbidden). The interaction doc expands the Tools section with per-tier permissions (which tier the agent can read / propose / edit / scaffold / archive). Use `templates/agent-vault-permissions.md.template` for the per-tier permission matrix.
- `methodology/03b-decide-operator-agent-interaction.md` — the agent SOUL has an "Operator priority" dimension. The operator-agent doc covers how the operator interacts with the agent (the 5 operator roles, the chat-output-budget rule, the escalation chain). Use `templates/operator-interaction-patterns.md.template` for the operator's role distribution per agent.

- `methodology/01a-decide-memory.md` — **the agent SOUL is identity memory (Tier 3).** The SOUL is the agent's contract with the operator; ≤1-2 pages is the budget. Use `templates/memory-budget.md.template` for the per-agent budget.

## Approval

- [ ] Identity is specific (name, role, owner, domain)
- [ ] Boundaries are non-negotiable and listed
- [ ] Tools list is default-deny (forbidden list is non-trivial)
- [ ] Skills list is short (1-3 always-load)
- [ ] Audit line is specific and brief
- [ ] Soul fits in 1-2 pages (longer = not ready)

Once all 6 boxes are checked, the soul is ready. Scaffold the agent.
